Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(hub): remove breadcrumb/streak and restyle cards to
 match reference
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two recent commits (6566339, 5b5e066) pushed the Learning Hub's look
away from what was actually wanted:

1. Header gained a 'Journey • <Region>' breadcrumb, a 'Learning Hub'
   label, and a 'Day 1 streak' indicator - none of these are in the
   reference design. Removed all three; header is now just back
   button, star counter, and the state name. Also dropped the now-
   unused regionName computation and its findRegionForState import.

2. Card styling drifted from the reference's clean look: every card
   had a solid-colored tinted background, a solid colored border, a
   solid colored circle badge with white text, and a solid colored
   arrow button on every card regardless of state. The reference only
   applies color (tinted background, colored border, solid arrow) to
   the single active/next-to-do card; every other card is plain white
   with a neutral border, a light pastel badge circle with colored
   text, and a light pastel arrow button with a plain chevron. Updated
   HubCard to match: color is now reserved for the active card only,
   and the progress label reads 'X/N questions' instead of 'X/N
   cards'.
